  "source": "[n_ \\.natural.+./ m_]\nDefines: n_ + m_ is \\binary.operation:on{\\naturals}\nexpresses:\n. piecewise:\n  if: n_ = 0\n  then: n_ + m_ := m_\n  else:\n  . let: k is \\natural\n    where: n_ = \\naturals..S(k)\n    then: n_ + m_ := \\naturals..S(n_ \\.natural.+./ k)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"$n_?$ plus $m_?$\"\n. written: \"n_? + m_?\"\n. description: \"Addition of natural numbers defined by recursion on the first\n                argument: $0 + m = m$ and $S(k) + m = S(k + m)$.\"\nId: \"a8dda59b-29db-4ac2-8d70-e9010ccae3e7\"",
